d520_cd3bdbcf",66,-14,1,"This should be TypeError, but you can also use `assert_throws_js(TypeError, ...)` to simplify."],["98542370_6e0d97c8",66,-14,1,"```suggestion }, \"piping a response into streamAppendHTMLUnsafe()\"); ```"],["a167a951_10127226",66,-14,1,"```suggestion }, \"writing a Symbol to streamAppendHTMLUnsafe()\"); ```"],["becfb2f7_1b9d60fe",67,-14,1,"Is it a problem that close() might be called twice and that we'll then call parser->Finish() twice? I guess not, but if parser were set to null here the question wouldn't arise."],["ccf603b9_6a6df777",66,-14,1,"Can you assert that it's just a single text node with the data \"12345\"?"],["dcd29fe8_c7ef416c",66,-14,1,"\"Conflicts\" are handled in a sense. How about just: ```suggestion }, \"Interleaved streamAppendHTMLUnsafe() writes\"); ```"],["df08abc9_5c87caba",66,-14,1,"```suggestion }, \"Aborting streamAppendHTMLUnsafe()\"); ```"],["e8b92682_cd4429d2",66,-14,1,"`currentPatch` is unused."],["f8c6766e_1a9b3b87",67,-14,1,"If document.streamAppendHTMLUnsafe() is just an alias for document.documentElement.streamAppendHTMLUnsafe() and DocumentFragment doesn't work, should we really have streamAppendHTMLUnsafe() on…"],["1ee8e174_72693c83",68,-12,0,"I don't love the name, but bikeshedding is bikeshedding."],["4e010685_cddf8c30",67,-12,1,"There might need (eventually) to be a way to specify the custom element registry."],["8afd28c7_3b49d447",67,-12,1,"PErhaps this should be in the constructor instead?"],["a299bc15_6aacf135",69,-12,1,"Could use a comment here explaining what this is."],["c8133d26_dc519726",67,-12,1,"CHECKs (even though they're not DCHECKs) shouldn't have side effects that matter."]],0,392],[7166870,20410,16,0.722,0.518,[[1,1.0,306,1733]],[],0,393],[7166711,20411,8,0.533,0.369,[[0,319]],[],0,394],[7186366,20414,1,0.169,0.112,[[0,320]],[],0,395],[7209122,20424,27,0.722,0.518,[[1,0.655,307,18],[0,0.345,321,9]],[["fd5de5af_9cedcac2",70,-1,1,"Instead of a test with a reference, can you add a -crash test? third_party/blink/web_tests/external/wpt/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-extreme-values-crash.html ``` <!DOCTYPE html> <link…"]],0,396],[7215437,20426,755,11.209,9.159,[[1,0.942,308,713],[0,0.058,322,42]],[["2a5e5fd6_c88fecab",71,0,1,"nit: indentation I think we are missing a restore too."],["5abb499f_d5478111",71,0,1,"`> Infinity` is always false"],["7ac4b7da_d7c76799",71,0,1,"nit: returns a DOMPoint (or change the code to return a DOMPointReadOnly)."],["b27e31dc_6bbd5bc1",72,0,0,"Similar question here: should any of this be guarded by the flag?"],["fc49be31_0e44b800",52,0,0,"This isn't guarded by the flag. Is this a no-op due to the \"without it shadow rects wouldn't have an origin rect\" part of the change description?"]],0,397],[7214810,20426,13,0.533,0.369,[[0,323]],[],0,398],[7224616,20427,19,0.722,0.518,[[4,0.455,9,9],[1,0.455,309,9],[0,0.091,324,1]],[["46efda0a_1341b784",73,-1,0,"This is surprising to see, after reading the I2S. I don't think it's a big deal, but can you update the I2S thread and mention that you're also shipping this?"]],0,399],[7222931,20428,129,4.229,3.289,[[1,0.746,310,100],[0,0.239,325,28],[4,0.014,10,1]],[["d3e06db0_0e0d73ef",74,-1,1,"Does this 100ms delay actually run? If so, can we avoid that or at least shorten it?"]],0,400],[7216031,20430,79,2.282,1.723,[[1,0.512,311,39],[0,0.488,326,40]],[],0,401],[7232017,20430,1,0.169,0.112,[[0,327]],[],0,402],[7224151,20430,65,2.282,1.723,[[1,0.971,312,64],[0,0.029,328,1]],[["467ca572_86193937",75,-4,1,"Shouldn't the ref just have no animation? It looks like this ref is identical to the test."],["6c2c85a5_da3691fb",76,-4,1,"Can you add a test where the underlying value is round? test_interpolation and test_composition take an underlying key to specify the underlying value."]],0,403],[7242324,20431,195,4.229,3.289,[[1,0.873,313,175],[0,0.113,329,18],[4,0.015,11,2]],[["0662296e_10413978",55,0,0,"Cool, synchronously remove children before returning."]],0,404],[7241391,20433,22,0.251,0.